MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
Three of the conditions compare numbers, and they differ only at
equality: GR is false there, GE is true, and EN is true only there.
There is no less-than in the vocabulary, so a test that wants one
writes its two arguments the other way round.
MCDEF REPORT,; AS <%A1. %A2.: MCGO L1 IF %A1. GR %A2.
not <>%L1.GR, MCGO L2 IF %A1. GE %A2.
not <>%L2.GE, MCGO L3 IF %A1. EN %A2.
not <>%L3.EN>
REPORT 4,3;
REPORT 3,3;
REPORT 2,3;
REPORT -6,-6;
The label of a jump is a macro expression as well, so a variable can
name the destination and the jump becomes a table. Arithmetic is
allowed there too, which is how a table is given a base.
MCDEF PICK; AS <MCSET T1=%A1.
MCGO LT1
%L1.first<>MCGO L0
%L2.second<>MCGO L0
%L3.third>
PICK 2;
PICK 3;
PICK 1;
MCDEF SIZE; AS <MCSET T1=%A1.
MCGO L T1 + 10 IF T1 GE 1
%L10.none<>MCGO L0
%L11.one<>MCGO L0
%L12.a pair<>MCGO L0
%L13.several>
SIZE 0;
SIZE 1;
SIZE 3;
